{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"Commands","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"externalID":"s:11WorldModule8CommandsV","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Commands.swift#L55","fileName":"Commands.swift"}},"abstract":[{"text":"A buffer of changes to a world, recorded now and applied later in the order they were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"recorded.","type":"text"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Commands","kind":"identifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/QueryingAWorld"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a query or an update visits a world’s entities, the world can’t be changed in other"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ways: spawning or despawning an entity, or adding or removing a component, would disturb the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage being visited. Record such changes in a command buffer instead, and apply them with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once the visit is over. The following example despawns every entity whose"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"health has run out:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["var world = World()","world.spawn(Health(current: 0))","world.spawn(Health(current: 10))","","var commands = Commands()","for (entity, health) in world.query(Health.self) where health.current <= 0 {","    commands.despawn(entity)","}","world.apply(commands)","","print(world.count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A command on an entity that is no longer live when it applies does nothing, so two commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that despawn the same entity are safe.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Naming-Entities-That-Commands-Will-Spawn","type":"heading","text":"Naming Entities That Commands Will Spawn"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)"},{"text":" returns a placeholder handle for the entity it will create. Later commands in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"same buffer can name that placeholder, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/apply(_:)"},{"text":" returns the real handles of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entities it spawned, in the order their commands were recorded:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","var commands = Commands()","let ship = commands.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 0))","let turret = commands.spawn(Position(x: 1, y: 0))","commands.addChild(turret, to: ship)","","let spawned = world.apply(commands)","print(world.parent(of: spawned[1]) == spawned[0])","\/\/ Prints \"true\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A placeholder stands for its entity only inside the buffer that returned it; the world holds no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entity with that handle."}]},{"level":3,"anchor":"Commands-from-Systems","type":"heading","text":"Commands from Systems"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A system running alongside others can’t apply commands itself, because applying them would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"change entities the other systems are reading. It queues them with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/queue(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instead, and the schedule applies every queued buffer at the end of each wave of systems.","type":"text"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"topicSections":[{"title":"Creating a Command Buffer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/init()"],"anchor":"Creating-a-Command-Buffer"},{"title":"Inspecting a Command Buffer","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/count","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/isEmpty"],"anchor":"Inspecting-a-Command-Buffer"},{"title":"Spawning and Despawning Entities","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/clone(_:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/spawn(from:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/despawn(_:)"],"anchor":"Spawning-and-Despawning-Entities"},{"title":"Adding and Removing Components","identifiers":["doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/insert(_:into:)","doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Commands\/remove(_: